@tjaychen 

as discussed, please clarify how it actually protects in this countermeasure - KEYMGR.SIDE_LOAD_SEL.CTRL.CONSISTENCY.

Also, the `KEYMGR.KMAC_IF_CMD.CTRL.CONSISTENCY` also does a consistency check [here](https://cs.opensource.google/opentitan/opentitan/+/master:hw/ip/keymgr/rtl/keymgr_kmac_if.sv;l=357?q=KMAC_IF_CMD.CTRL.CONSISTENCY%09%20&ss=opentitan%2Fopentitan:hw%2F) (during an operation, changing one type of operation to another one will trigger the error), but the spec only mentions the one-hot check.

fix_patch:
