resolved_issues.body:
Hi @tjaychen 

I have been debugging a regression fail isssue in the flash_ctrl_host_ctrl_arb test (which I believe I have solved).

However, when I rebased the code base to the latest, I now see different errors from this test.  

After the RMA has completed, the ACK goes On, then one cycle later goes Off again, and the state_q changes from StHw->StSwIdle->StInvalid, and we get a fatal error.

(waves enclosed)

I think this is because the RTL has changed as below (MuBi)

If this is already documented, then I may have missed this.

At the moment I do not know whats is causing this ... but obviously will investigate.

Obviously something due to the changes below

If you can assist, that would be great

RTL File : flash_ctrl_host_ctrl_arb.sv

NEW CODE

      StSwIdle: begin
        // software is still selected to enable access to Fifos
        func_sel = SwSel;

        if (prim_mubi_pkg::mubi4_test_true_loose(disable_i)) begin
          // Do not randomly switch unless idle as it may cause stateful operations to be
          // disturbed
          state_d = StInvalid;
        end else if (hw_req_i) begin
          // if hardware request comes in the middle, wipe fifos and enable
          // switch to hardware interface
          fifo_clr_o = 1'b1;
          state_d = StHw;
        end else if (sw_req) begin
          state_d = StSwActive;
        end
      end

OLD CODE

      StSwIdle: begin
        // software is still selected to enable access to Fifos
        func_sel = SwSel;

        // if hardware request comes in the middle, wipe fifos and enable
        // switch to hardware interface
        if (hw_req_i) begin
          fifo_clr_o = 1'b1;
          state_d = StHw;
        end else if (sw_req) begin
          state_d = StSwActive;
        end
      end

![Screen Shot 03-31-22 at 05 51 PM](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/92723163/161108836-fe4ec7aa-a04e-4640-a7e5-11c905780a3d.PNG)

